---
// Fig. for "Subgroups, Cosets, Roots of Unity & Vanishing Polynomials": the
// size-4 subgroup found earlier is exactly the set of 4th roots of unity
// mod 13 — the numbers whose 4th power is 1 — and one number, 5, generates
// all of them.
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 544" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">the numbers that return to 1</text>

  <rect x="40" y="38" width="680" height="44" rx="9" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="65" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c3cedd" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">Which numbers x satisfy x<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 1, mod 13?</tspan></text>

  <text x="40" y="108" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 1 &#8212; test candidates</text>
  <text x="380" y="130" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">1<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 1 &#10003;</tspan></text>
  <text x="380" y="152" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">5<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 625 = 48&#215;13 + 1 &#10003;</tspan></text>
  <text x="380" y="174" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">8<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 4096 = 315&#215;13 + 1 &#10003;</tspan></text>
  <text x="380" y="196" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">12<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = (&#8722;1)</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 1 &#10003;</tspan></text>
  <text x="380" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ff5c7a" font-size="14" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">2<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 16 = 3 &#10007;</tspan></text>

  <line x1="40" y1="238" x2="720" y2="238" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />

  <text x="40" y="264" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 2 &#8212; name them</text>
  <text x="380" y="288" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14.5" font-weight="700" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">&#123;1, 5, 12, 8&#125; are the 4th roots of unity</text>
  <text x="380" y="308" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="11.5" font-style="italic" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">(a polynomial of degree 4 has at most 4 roots)</text>

  <line x1="40" y1="326" x2="720" y2="326" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />

  <text x="40" y="352" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 3 &#8212; one number generates them</text>
  <text x="380" y="376" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="14" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">&#969; = 5:  5<tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">1</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 5,  5</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">2</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 12,  5</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">3</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 8,  5</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="70%">4</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 1</tspan></text>

  <rect x="140" y="396" width="480" height="46" rx="10" fill="#0d1a12" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="2" />
  <text x="380" y="424" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14.5" font-weight="800" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">domain = &#123;&#969;<tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">0</tspan><tspan dy="5">, &#969;</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">1</tspan><tspan dy="5">, &#969;</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="5">, &#969;</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">3</tspan><tspan dy="5">&#125; = &#123;1, 5, 12, 8&#125;</tspan></text>

  <text x="380" y="466" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">5<tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = 12 = &#8722;1, just like i</tspan><tspan dy="-5" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="5"> = &#8722;1</tspan></text>

  <line x1="40" y1="484" x2="720" y2="484" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="508" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">ROOTS OF UNITY ARE POWERS OF ONE SPECIAL NUMBER</text>
  <text x="380" y="528" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">n-th roots of unity exist mod p exactly when n divides p &#8722; 1.</text>
</svg>
